ci_doc_regeneration_increment: A temp-directory-only edit of release configure can invalidate Automake stamp-vti even though no Texinfo or configure template changes. The resulting old mdate-sh parsing failure and makeinfo error are a new downstream phase, not a reason to reject valid HAVE_FEATURE definitions or disable the detected SSH/readline features.
ci_doc_regeneration_repair: Save configure atime_ns/mtime_ns before the three strict OHOS tempdir replacements and restore only that file's original release timestamps with os.utime. Preserve the VTI dependency rule and shipped doc bytes; changed configure.ac/Texinfo input still needs genuine regeneration and a real toolchain.
ci_doc_regeneration_boundary: Reuses E248 timestamp reasoning and DRAFT-11103-teseq-mdate-sh-iso-date-vti causal chain, but unlike a permanent no-op VTI rule does not disable future legitimate documentation regeneration. Do not suppress makeinfo errors or skip make check; this remedy only applies to a generated-script execution-policy edit with unchanged templates/documentation.
ci_doc_regeneration_failure_evidence: yafc-w3-20261012-hmdfs-tmp-recipe-r2 failed at make check: mdate-sh could not parse ls output, version.texi updated, then makeinfo missing. Official archive configure mtime1451669051 precedes stamp-vti/version.texi1451669095 and yafc.info1451669096; doc/Makefile.in stamp-vti explicitly depends on configure.
ci_doc_regeneration_pass_evidence: yafc-w3-20261012-hmdfs-tmp-recipe-r3 official local CI exit0; make check fully executed with no registered upstream tests; installed CLI/FTP consumers6/6; 12 receipts and release/postrelease PASS. Full finishRC1 only step5b/step8, not claimed overallPASS. Raw log SHA256629d330931e04fa55ed92491eb9640b818fe290ca012b0b6492d19b2c14e0214.
